Third-party notices for the myna-text snap
==========================================

Model components
----------------

model-disfluency-en: a multilingual MiniLM-based disfluency tagger fine-tuned
by Canonical Ltd (Apache-2.0) from Microsoft's Multilingual-MiniLM-L12-H384
(MIT, with XLM-RoBERTa's MIT vocabulary) on text derived from SODA and
Synthetic-Persona-Chat (both CC-BY-4.0) for English and from Tatoeba sentences
(CC BY 2.0 FR) for French, German and Spanish. The component carries the full
attribution (NOTICE) and the Apache-2.0 text (LICENSE).

Runtimes
--------

The Python runtime of the daemon (onnxruntime, tokenizers, numpy and their
dependencies) is installed from PyPI at the versions and hashes pinned in the
Myna source tree's server/uv.lock; their licence files travel in their
distributions.
